<XDFFORMAT version="1.70">
  <XDFHEADER>
    <flags>0x1</flags>
    <description>Suzuki Hayabusa Gen 3 (RH850/E1L) - full 2 MB reads 5JCZSJ40 (32990-10L4) and 5JCZSJ10 (32990-10L1). Every table comes from the ECU map-descriptor list (all 746 descriptor-backed tables cross-checked against the descriptors: addresses, counts and 8/16-bit sizes). Scales: RPM = X/2.56; throttle and grip angle = X/364.08 deg; pressure kPa = (X-7862)/393.14 (stock internal scale - still valid on SD-v3 for every stock table); 8-bit temperature C = X*0.9375-30; ignition deg = (X-64)*0.3516.

RACE SOFTWARE XDF (SD-v3 and later). Speed-density fuel and the boost spark map read the RAW IAP sensor ADC (fef02574, 10-bit) so they cover the full 3-bar range; their axes display kPa via X*0.307429-12.6 (provisional 3-bar transfer, 62.9 kPa/V, -12.6 kPa, 204.6 counts/V). If you recalibrate the sensor, change that equation on the 8 SD maps and 2 boost spark maps and recompute IAP GAIN/OFFSET (see those constants). The rest of the ECU stays on the stock internal pressure scale (IAP saturates at ~147 kPa there by design). Checksums: field 1 = CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE (poly 0x1021, init 0xFFFF, no reflect, no xorout) over 0x10000-0x1FFAFB, stored big-endian at 0x1FFAFE. Field 3 (0x1FFEF8) is not recomputed. Use only with Hayabusa-5JCZSJ40-race-software-SD-v4.bin (or later SD bins built the same way); on a stock bin the SD and boost-spark axes display wrong.

SD-v4 ROLLING ANTI-LAG: hold the START button while rolling (front wheel &gt;= min speed); go WOT and the ECU captures the current RPM and holds it with an all-cylinder SPARK cut (fuel stays on) plus the "ALS Timing Retard" map, until the button is released, the grip is rolled back, or the max-time safety trips. Holding START while rolling no longer reaches the stock launch-control long-press (blocked by the patch). Settings: category "Rolling Anti-Lag (SD-v4)". Code lives at 0xBE000-0xBE147 (do not edit), calibration at 0xBF000-0xBF00F, state RAM 0xFEBFE000.</description>
    <BASEOFFSET offset="0" subtract="0" />
    <DEFAULTS datasizeinbits="8" sigdigits="2" outputtype="1" signed="0" lsbfirst="1" float="0" />
