  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1001" flags="0x0">
    <title>Gear :: Curve [Gear] 7pt FUN_2a696 #005</title>
    <description>Gear-dependent setting. The gear axis is a bitmask: 1 = Neutral, 2 = 1st, 4 = 2nd, 8 = 3rd, 16 = 4th, 32 = 5th, 64 = 6th. (Family-level description - specific use not individually confirmed.)

HOW THE ECU USES IT: looked up by FUN_2a696; X input = Gear position bitmask (1=N, 2=1st ... 0x40=6th) from GP sensor ADC ch2E (RAM 0xFEF026C2).

AXES: X axis: 7 points, 1.00 to 64.0 gear bit.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ40): 432 to 65535 raw.

REFERENCE: data @0x151300, X axis @0x150570, descriptor @0x150878, code FUN_2a696.</description>
