  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x10C3" flags="0x0">
    <title>SD (abs MAP) - In Gear | Cyl 4</title>
    <description>SPEED-DENSITY base fuel, cylinder 4, In Gear. Output = raw fuel quantity (injection time units) vs manifold ABSOLUTE pressure and RPM.

HOW THE ECU USES IT (SD-v3): looked up by FUN_45320 (map 0 of the cylinder set; maps 1-5 are never blended - weight is hard 0). X input = RAW IAP sensor ADC fef02574 (code patch); axis shown in kPa via X*0.307429-12.6 (provisional 3-bar calibration). Fuel authority: blend curve and WOT gate are 0xFFFF, so this map fuels the engine at all throttle openings except sensor-fault limp-home (throttle path).

AXES: X 30 points, 20-300 kPa abs; Y 50 points, 800-16000 RPM.

STARTING VALUES: below 101 kPa = this cylinder's stock IAP map interpolated onto the new axis; above 101 kPa = density-scaled from the stock 0-vacuum column (which stock never actually fuelled from at WOT). Starting point only - tune on a wideband.

REFERENCE: data @0x1675B0, X axis @0x156034, Y axis @0x16754C, descriptor @0x156070, code FUN_45320.</description>
