  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x10D3" flags="0x0">
    <title>TPS - In Gear | Cyl 2</title>
    <description>Main alpha-N (throttle based) base fuel map for cylinder 2 while in gear with the clutch released. Output is a raw fuel quantity (injection time units) indexed by throttle angle and RPM.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: Code: FUN_4536c looks up all six maps of the cylinder 2 set (pointer table 0x17EBE4, index cyl*6+n); FUN_453B8 then uses map 1 as the result, blended with map 2 by a weight that is hard-coded to 0, so this map is the one that actually fuels cylinder 2. In neutral / clutch-in the "TPS - Neutral/Clutch-In | Cyl 2" map is used instead. Was "TPS - Mode B | Gear 1" in the DanCycles naming.

AXES: X axis: 26 points, 0.46 to 118 deg (abs. TP angle); Y axis: 50 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ40): 454 to 5132 raw (inj. time?).

TUNING NOTES: This is the cylinder 2 TPS fuel map you would normally tune. Changes here affect cylinder 2 only, so keep the four cylinder maps consistent unless you are correcting a cylinder-to-cylinder imbalance. How the TPS and IAP results are combined downstream has not been traced yet - change one family at a time and log.

CONFIDENCE: Cylinder assignment confirmed from code (cyl*6 indexing) and from data (stock cylinder-to-cylinder offsets match the Neutral/Clutch-In Cyl 1-4 maps exactly in the same order).

REFERENCE: data @0x172E70, X axis @0x156584, Y axis @0x172E0C, descriptor @0x1565B8, code FUN_4536c.</description>
