  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x112E" flags="0x0">
    <title>IGN :: Trim A | Neutral/Clutch-In</title>
    <description>Ignition timing trim map (throttle angle x RPM, 8-bit). 64 raw = 0 deg (no change).

HOW THE ECU USES IT: Used instead of the Trim A select maps while in neutral (or clutch pulled, if option 0x18B761 = 0x80). Looked up by FUN_52526 / FUN_525EE / FUN_525A0 / FUN_5262A (throttle angle 0xFEF02602 x RPM 0xFEF0155C); all trim outputs and the base advance are initialised to 64 (0x40) in FUN_51B02, confirming 64 = neutral.

AXES: X axis: 23 points, 0.00 to 117 deg (abs. TP angle); Y axis: 39 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ40): -3.87 to 32.7 deg (trim, 64 raw = 0).

TUNING NOTES: Values ABOVE 64 RETARD, below 64 advance (traced in FUN_517B4/FUN_5171C/FUN_5275A). Trim D (fef01578) is subtracted directly from the main advance path; Trims A, B and C feed a MAX-of-retards selector (fef01569) that is subtracted. Change carefully and log knock/timing.

CONFIDENCE: Selection logic confirmed; per-count scale 0.3516 deg taken from the OBD timing-advance encoding (assumes trims use the same units as final advance). Was "IGN :: Offset Timing - 1".

REFERENCE: data @0x187404, X axis @0x18483C, Y axis @0x186DC4, descriptor @0x18307C, code FUN_52526.</description>
