  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1132" flags="0x0">
    <title>ALS Timing Retard (MAP x RPM)</title>
    <description>IGNITION RETARD used while rolling anti-lag is ACTIVE (replaces the boost retard map during ALS). SD-v4: FUN_525EE now selects this map when ALS is active (code hook at 0x525F2 -&gt; ALS_IS_ACTIVE) and the "Boost Spark Retard - In Gear" map at all other times, including neutral/clutch-in. Same signal path as boost retard: value above 64 = degrees of retard, applied as a retard floor (MAX of retard requests). DEFAULT: max(20 deg, boost retard) in every cell. More retard = hotter exhaust, faster spool, more stress on turbo/exhaust valves.

REFERENCE: data @0x188214, X axis @0x1848FC (raw IAP ADC, shown in kPa), Y axis @0x186F04, descriptor @0x1830EC.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="11" /><CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="13" /><CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="54" /><XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
