  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1134" flags="0x0">
    <title>IGN :: Trim C | Select 1 (gear 1)</title>
    <description>Ignition timing trim map (throttle angle x RPM, 8-bit). 64 raw = 0 deg (no change).

HOW THE ECU USES IT: Chosen by per-gear selector bytes 0x18B762-0x18B767 = 1. Stock: 1st gear. Looked up by FUN_52526 / FUN_525EE / FUN_525A0 / FUN_5262A (throttle angle 0xFEF02602 x RPM 0xFEF0155C); all trim outputs and the base advance are initialised to 64 (0x40) in FUN_51B02, confirming 64 = neutral.

AXES: X axis: 23 points, 0.00 to 117 deg (abs. TP angle); Y axis: 39 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ40): 0.00 to 0.00 deg (trim, 64 raw = 0) - every cell is the same (0.00), so the function is probably disabled or unused in this calibration.

TUNING NOTES: Values ABOVE 64 RETARD, below 64 advance (traced in FUN_517B4/FUN_5171C/FUN_5275A). Trim D (fef01578) is subtracted directly from the main advance path; Trims A, B and C feed a MAX-of-retards selector (fef01569) that is subtracted. Change carefully and log knock/timing.

CONFIDENCE: Selection logic confirmed; per-count scale 0.3516 deg taken from the OBD timing-advance encoding (assumes trims use the same units as final advance). Was "IGN :: Offset Timing - 7".

REFERENCE: data @0x18891C, X axis @0x18495C, Y axis @0x186FA4, descriptor @0x183124, code FUN_525a0.</description>
