  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1148" flags="0x0">
    <title>TC - Target Slip | Level 1 | 1st</title>
    <description>Traction-control TARGET SLIP for TC level 1, 1st gear: how much rear-wheel slip is allowed before TC intervenes, as a function of estimated drive acceleration.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_4D602 selects the curve by TC level (RAM 0xFEF026D4, set by the ride mode preset / user mode, 1-10) and gear (gear bitmask 0xFEF026C2; 6th gear and neutral use the last entry); a separate set is used when the launch-control flag (0xFEF00702 bit6) is active. Input = estimated drive acceleration (RAM 0xFEF009D0 = engine-torque map x gear ratio / tyre radius - drag). Output -&gt; RAM 0xFEF0134A. FUN_4DBD6 then computes slip error = (rear - front)/front x1000 - target, which drives the torque-cut curves.

AXES: X axis: 21 points, -1606 to 14460 raw (0x8000=0).

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ40): 8.00 to 18.0 % target slip.

TUNING NOTES: Higher values allow more slip before TC cuts power (less intrusive). Change the matching level/gear only; the TC level actually used comes from the ride mode (A=1, B=5, C=10 in this calibration) or the user setting.

CONFIDENCE: Traced in the decompiled code (functions and RAM addresses given above); physical scaling of intermediate values partly inferred.

REFERENCE: data @0x184DB0, X axis @0x184D84, descriptor @0x183378, code FUN_4d602.</description>
