    <description>Traction-control TARGET SLIP for TC level 4, 3rd gear: how much rear-wheel slip is allowed before TC intervenes, as a function of estimated drive acceleration.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_4D602 selects the curve by TC level (RAM 0xFEF026D4, set by the ride mode preset / user mode, 1-10) and gear (gear bitmask 0xFEF026C2; 6th gear and neutral use the last entry); a separate set is used when the launch-control flag (0xFEF00702 bit6) is active. Input = estimated drive acceleration (RAM 0xFEF009D0 = engine-torque map x gear ratio / tyre radius - drag). Output -&gt; RAM 0xFEF0134A. FUN_4DBD6 then computes slip error = (rear - front)/front x1000 - target, which drives the torque-cut curves.

