  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x119D" flags="0x0">
    <title>TC - Cut vs Slip Rate | Level 1</title>
    <description>Traction-control derivative term for TC level 1: torque cut vs how fast the slip error is changing.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_4DDFC looks this up with RAM 0xFEF0135C (moving-average change of slip, 0x8000 = steady, from FUN_4CD6A). Used instead of the next curve depending on flags 0xFEF013A8 bit7 / 0xFEF013A9 bit0.

AXES: X axis: 9 points, 205 to 860 raw (0x8000=0).

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ40): 32768 to 32768 raw - every cell is the same (32768), so the function is probably disabled or unused in this calibration.

TUNING NOTES: Makes TC react to rapidly rising slip before the slip itself is large.

CONFIDENCE: Traced in the decompiled code (functions and RAM addresses given above); physical scaling of intermediate values partly inferred.

