  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x119F" flags="0x0">
    <title>TC - Lean Gain | Level 1</title>
    <description>Lean-angle gain on the slip-error cut for TC level 1.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_4DDFC multiplies the "Cut vs Slip Error" result by this value / 100 at the current lean angle (RAM 0xFEF0268E). Forced to 100 % when slip error exceeds the per-level threshold 0x18B6E4.

AXES: X axis: 9 points, 0.00 to 60.0 deg (est.).

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ40): 100 to 100 % of slip-error cut - every cell is the same (100), so the function is probably disabled or unused in this calibration.

TUNING NOTES: Values below 100 soften the cut while leaned (or above 100 to strengthen it).

CONFIDENCE: Traced in the decompiled code (functions and RAM addresses given above); physical scaling of intermediate values partly inferred.

REFERENCE: data @0x186660, X axis @0x18664C, descriptor @0x183B5C, code FUN_4ddfc.</description>
