    <title>TC - Ignition Retard | Band 1</title>
    <description>Traction-control ignition retard map for cut-demand band 1 of 10 (throttle angle x RPM).

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_4E2B4 converts the TC cut demand into a band position (RAM 0xFEF0137E = demand x 0xA000 / const 0x18B702; band 1 covers 0x0-0x1000) and interpolates between this map and the next. Result -&gt; RAM 0xFEF013A6/A7 -&gt; per-cylinder TC retard 0xFEF0157E-81, which FUN_4189E subtracts from the final ignition timing of each cylinder.

AXES: X axis: 10 points, 0.46 to 112 deg (abs. TP angle); Y axis: 6 points, 2000 to 11000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ40): 0.00 to 12.3 deg retard.

TUNING NOTES: Bigger values = more retard (more torque reduction) at that cut level. Scale assumes the same 0.3516 deg/count as the timing maps.

