    <description>Anti-lift (wheelie control) THROTTLE limit map - Stage B Entry | PWR 1.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_7C62A picks the map from the anti-lift stage counters (RAM 0xFEF00A13 = stage A step 1-4, 0xFEF00A14 = stage B step 1-4; "Entry" = first step, "Hold" = later steps) and, for stage B, the active throttle slot / power mode (0xFEF026D3). X = RPM (0xFEF02AD4), Y = current final ignition timing (0xFEF01567, so throttle closing is coordinated with the ignition retard). FUN_7C944 applies the result as min(limit, normal throttle target) in ETV state 3 (set when the anti-lift flags 0xFEF0096F bit5/6 are on).

