debits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9033" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 2</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 2 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6EE" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9034" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 3</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 3 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6F0" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9035" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 4</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 4 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6F2" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9036" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 5</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 5 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6F4" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9037" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 6</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 6 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6F6" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9038" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 7</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 7 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6F8" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9039" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 8</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 8 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6FA" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x903A" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 9</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 9 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6FC" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x903B" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Level 10</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC level 10 (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B6FE" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x903C" flags="0x0"><title>TC Max Cut | Launch</title><description>Upper limit on the total TC cut demand for TC launch (FUN_4DDFC, applied when flag 0xFEF013A9 bit3 is set).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B700" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x903D" flags="0x0"><title>TC Cut Band Scale</title><description>Divisor used by FUN_4E140 to convert TC cut demand into the 10 ignition-retard bands: band position = demand x 0xA000 / this value.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B702" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x903E" flags="0x0"><title>TC Slip-Error Gain</title><description>Gain applied to the slip error in FUN_4DBD6 (x/16).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B7C4" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x903F" flags="0x0"><title>TC Lean Offset Enable</title><description>0x80 = use the lean-angle slip-offset curves (fef01358); other = use fef01354. Read in FUN_4DBD6.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="46" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18B7C3" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units /><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9801" flags="0x0"><title>Rev Limiter (in gear) | Fuel Cut ON</title><description>Main in-gear rev limiter - fuel is cut when RPM reaches this value. State machine FUN_2C73E: with the gear sensor in a valid gear and clutch released (FUN_2C3F2) and option 0x154447 != 0x80, state 2 runs FUN_2C652. Engine speed = RAM 0xFEF0258C. Cut type: FUEL (all injectors, primary + secondary) via cut-request flag 0xFEF00A30 bit1 -&gt; per-cylinder fuel-cut mode 0xFEF011A8 = 1 (FUN_4BAAE / FUN_477B0). Ignition and throttle are not touched by this limiter. Keep ON above OFF (hysteresis). Raising this raises the redline cut; the Ignition-Cut Limiter (12,000) sits above it as a backstop, so raising past ~11,900 also needs that pair raised.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 11200 RPM (raw 28672/0x7000).

REFERENCE: @0x1542C6.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542C6" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9802" flags="0x0"><title>Rev Limiter (in gear) | Fuel Cut OFF (resume)</title><description>Fuel is restored when RPM falls below this value (FUN_2C652). Keep it ~100 rpm below the ON value. Engine speed = RAM 0xFEF0258C. Cut type: FUEL (all injectors, primary + secondary) via cut-request flag 0xFEF00A30 bit1 -&gt; per-cylinder fuel-cut mode 0xFEF011A8 = 1 (FUN_4BAAE / FUN_477B0). Ignition and throttle are not touched by this limiter.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 11100 RPM (raw 28416/0x6F00).

REFERENCE: @0x1542C4.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542C4" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9803" flags="0x0"><title>Rev Limiter (neutral / clutch) | Fuel Cut ON</title><description>Limiter used when not in a valid gear (neutral, or clutch pulled), state 3 after the debounce counter 0xFEF00A20 &gt;= 0x154448. Code: FUN_2C68C (and FUN_2C6C6, which uses the identical pair at 0x1542CC/CE). Engine speed = RAM 0xFEF0258C. Cut type: FUEL (all injectors, primary + secondary) via cut-request flag 0xFEF00A30 bit1 -&gt; per-cylinder fuel-cut mode 0xFEF011A8 = 1 (FUN_4BAAE / FUN_477B0). Ignition and throttle are not touched by this limiter.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 10800 RPM (raw 27648/0x6C00).

REFERENCE: @0x1542CA.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542CA" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9804" flags="0x0"><title>Rev Limiter (neutral / clutch) | Fuel Cut OFF</title><description>Resume point for the neutral/clutch limiter (FUN_2C68C).

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 10700 RPM (raw 27392/0x6B00).

REFERENCE: @0x1542C8.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542C8" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9805" flags="0x0"><title>Rev Limiter (neutral / clutch) alt | Fuel Cut ON</title><description>Second copy of the neutral limiter used by FUN_2C6C6 (alternate state-3 path). Stock = same as the main neutral pair - change both together.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 10800 RPM (raw 27648/0x6C00).

REFERENCE: @0x1542CE.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542CE" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9806" flags="0x0"><title>Rev Limiter (neutral / clutch) alt | Fuel Cut OFF</title><description>Resume point for FUN_2C6C6.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 10700 RPM (raw 27392/0x6B00).

REFERENCE: @0x1542CC.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542CC" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9807" flags="0x0"><title>Ignition-Cut Limiter | ON</title><description>Backstop limiter that is ALWAYS evaluated (FUN_2C700): sets 0xFEF00A19 bit2 -&gt; 0xFEF00A30 bit2 -&gt; ignition-cut mode 0xFEF01554 = 2 on all cylinders (FUN_4FBCC, coil outputs inhibited by FUN_50EE2). This is the only SPARK-cut limiter in the stock calibration.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 12000 RPM (raw 30720/0x7800).

REFERENCE: @0x1542D2.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542D2" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9808" flags="0x0"><title>Ignition-Cut Limiter | OFF</title><description>Spark restored below this RPM (FUN_2C700).

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 11900 RPM (raw 30464/0x7700).

REFERENCE: @0x1542D0.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542D0" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9809" flags="0x0"><title>Per-Gear Limiter | 3rd | Soft Cut start</title><description>Per-gear RPM limiter FUN_2C068 (enabled by option 0x15444B = 0x80; skipped in 1st and 2nd). From word 1 up to word 2 the ECU sets 0xFEF009C6 bit0 = soft (pattern) fuel cut; at or above words 3 and 4 it sets bit1 = full fuel cut (FUN_4BAAE). In stock this gear is set to 25,000+ rpm = disabled.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 25000 RPM (raw 64000/0xFA00).

REFERENCE: @0x1542D4.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542D4" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x980A" flags="0x0"><title>Per-Gear Limiter | 3rd | Soft Cut end / hard window</title><description>Per-gear RPM limiter FUN_2C068 (enabled by option 0x15444B = 0x80; skipped in 1st and 2nd). From word 1 up to word 2 the ECU sets 0xFEF009C6 bit0 = soft (pattern) fuel cut; at or above words 3 and 4 it sets bit1 = full fuel cut (FUN_4BAAE). In stock this gear is set to 25,000+ rpm = disabled.

