REFERENCE: @0x1542B0.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542B0" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9827" flags="0x0"><title>Progressive Limiter | Stage 4 ON (normal)</title><description>4-stage progressive fuel-cut limiter (FUN_2C5B0, state 1 - only used if option 0x154447 = 0x80). Stage 1-3 = partial cut using the cylinder mask 0x1826D8 and skip-pattern bytes 0x1826D9-0x1826E1 (FUN_4B85E / FUN_4BC76); stage 4 = full cut. STOCK: all 25,593-25,600 rpm and option = 0x00, i.e. DISABLED - the bike uses the simple on/off limiter instead.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 25600 RPM (raw 65535/0xFFFF).

REFERENCE: @0x1542C2.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542C2" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9828" flags="0x0"><title>Progressive Limiter | Stage 4 ON (warm-up)</title><description>Alternate thresholds for the progressive limiter used while the engine-temperature timer flag 0xFEF00A1E bit4 is set (FUN_2C7E8; ECT thresholds 0x154449/0x15444A). STOCK: disabled (25,600 rpm).

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 25600 RPM (raw 65535/0xFFFF).

REFERENCE: @0x1542B2.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542B2" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9829" flags="0x0"><title>Progressive Limiter Enable</title><description>Option byte read by FUN_2C4CC: 0x80 = in-gear limiting uses the 4-stage progressive limiter (state 1); anything else = simple on/off limiter (state 2). STOCK 0x00. Only switch to 0x80 after setting the progressive thresholds and a non-zero cut mask (0x1826D8).

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 0 raw (raw 0/0x0).

REFERENCE: @0x154447.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x154447" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x982A" flags="0x0"><title>Per-Gear Limiter Enable</title><description>0x80 = per-gear limiter FUN_2C068 active (stock 0x80 - required for the 6th-gear speed governor). Set to 0x00 to disable all per-gear limits.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 128 raw (raw 128/0x80).

REFERENCE: @0x15444B.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x15444B" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x982B" flags="0x0"><title>Partial-Cut Cylinder Mask</title><description>Bit mask used by FUN_4B85E when the progressive limiter is in stages 1-3: bit1 = cyl 1, bit2 = cyl 2, bit3 = cyl 3, bit4 = cyl 4. STOCK 0x00 = no cylinders, so the progressive soft-cut does nothing.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 0 raw (raw 0/0x0).

REFERENCE: @0x1826D8.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1826D8" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x982C" flags="0x0"><title>Fuel-Cut Gear-Sensor Fault Limit (max)</title><description>When the gear-position sensor reading is invalid (FUN_2C8E2 window checks) the ECU applies a limit from curve 0x1511EC vs rear-wheel speed, clamped between this value and the min below (FUN_2CB40).

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 11000 RPM (raw 28160/0x6E00).

REFERENCE: @0x1542A2.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542A2" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x982D" flags="0x0"><title>Fuel-Cut Gear-Sensor Fault Limit (min)</title><description>Lower clamp for the gear-sensor-fault limiter (FUN_2CB40).

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 3000 RPM (raw 7680/0x1E00).

REFERENCE: @0x1542A0.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="27" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1542A0" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x982E" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control | Level 1 | Soft Cut start</title><description>Launch-control RPM limiter, level 1, threshold 1 of 4. Code: FUN_28E5E copies the 4 words for the selected LC level (RAM 0xFEF026D9 = 1/2/3) into 0xFEF009DA-E0; FUN_2BD08 then runs a staged limiter while LC is active (0xFEF00702 bit5). Word 1-3 = soft zone: 0xFEF009C1 bit1 -&gt; per-cylinder pattern fuel cut (FUN_4B9DA -&gt; 0xFEF01309 -&gt; fuel-cut mode 3, skip pattern from 0x1826D9-0x1826E1). Word 4 = hard limit: 0xFEF009C1 bit0 -&gt; full fuel cut on all injectors. No spark cut and no timing retard is used by the LC RPM limiter; throttle is capped separately by the "Launch Control - Throttle Limit" maps. Keep the four values ascending. Stock spacing is ~25-75 rpm.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 3623 RPM (raw 9275/0x243B).

