REFERENCE: @0x154488.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x154488" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x983B" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control Gear Mask</title><description>Gears in which LC can arm (bitmask vs RAM 0xFEF026C2: 0x01 = neutral, 0x02 = 1st, 0x04 = 2nd ...). Stock 0x03 = neutral + 1st.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 3 raw (raw 3/0x3).

REFERENCE: @0x154489.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x154489" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x983C" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control | Level 1 | Use Launch TC/Anti-lift sets</title><description>0x80 = while LC level 1 is active, switch traction control to its "Launch" curve set (FUN_28D30 -&gt; 0xFEF00702 bit6, used by the TC functions FUN_4D602 etc.) and anti-lift to its launch parameters 0x154340-0x154343 / 0x154480-0x154483 (FUN_28D8C -&gt; bit7, FUN_29BC4). Stock 0x00 = OFF for all levels, so stock LC uses the normal TC / anti-lift level.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 0 raw (raw 0/0x0).

REFERENCE: @0x15448D.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x15448D" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x983D" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control | Level 2 | Use Launch TC/Anti-lift sets</title><description>0x80 = while LC level 2 is active, switch traction control to its "Launch" curve set (FUN_28D30 -&gt; 0xFEF00702 bit6, used by the TC functions FUN_4D602 etc.) and anti-lift to its launch parameters 0x154340-0x154343 / 0x154480-0x154483 (FUN_28D8C -&gt; bit7, FUN_29BC4). Stock 0x00 = OFF for all levels, so stock LC uses the normal TC / anti-lift level.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 0 raw (raw 0/0x0).

REFERENCE: @0x15448E.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x15448E" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x983E" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control | Level 3 | Use Launch TC/Anti-lift sets</title><description>0x80 = while LC level 3 is active, switch traction control to its "Launch" curve set (FUN_28D30 -&gt; 0xFEF00702 bit6, used by the TC functions FUN_4D602 etc.) and anti-lift to its launch parameters 0x154340-0x154343 / 0x154480-0x154483 (FUN_28D8C -&gt; bit7, FUN_29BC4). Stock 0x00 = OFF for all levels, so stock LC uses the normal TC / anti-lift level.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 0 raw (raw 0/0x0).

REFERENCE: @0x15448F.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x15448F" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x983F" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control | Release detect wheel-speed</title><description>Front AND rear wheel speed must exceed this (X/128 = km/h) before the post-launch counter runs (FUN_289C4 / FUN_28A42).

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 10 km/h (raw 1280/0x500).

REFERENCE: @0x154358.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x154358" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>km/h</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/128"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9840" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control | Release detect grip angle</title><description>Grip (APS) angle threshold used by FUN_28A42 for the post-launch phase (X/364.08 deg).

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 22 deg (raw 7864/0x1EB8).

REFERENCE: @0x15435C.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x15435C" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>deg</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/364.08"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9841" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control | RPM-limit release speed</title><description>FUN_28B50: the LC RPM limiter (0xFEF00702 bit5) stays applied only while FRONT wheel speed is below this (X/128 km/h; stock 5 km/h). Once the bike is rolling the RPM cap is dropped and only the LC throttle-limit/phase-out remains until LC ends.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 5 km/h (raw 640/0x280).

REFERENCE: @0x154362.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x154362" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>km/h</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/128"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9842" flags="0x0"><title>Launch Control | Hold suspend timer</title><description>FUN_28BC6: if RAM 0xFEF0258E stays above the threshold at 0x18DA8E for this many counts (and condition FUN_73B52 is false) LC is suspended (flag 0xFEF00725 bit2) - most likely the hold-time protection that drops LC if it is held on the limiter too long. Exact signal unconfirmed.

STOCK: 5JCZSJ40 = 25 counts (raw 25/0x19).

REFERENCE: @0x15437E.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="24" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x15437E" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>counts</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA001" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P0607 - ECM performance (internal processor) - MIL enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the MIL when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 0, lamp byte @0x1B9684 (mask 0x01). CAUTION: safety-critical fault (throttle-by-wire, ECM integrity or oil pressure). Hiding its lamp means you will not be told when the ECU has gone into a throttle or engine fail-safe. Not recommended.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1B9684" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x01</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA002" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P2123 - APS (accelerator) sensor 1 high - MIL enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the MIL when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 1, lamp byte @0x1B9698 (mask 0x01). CAUTION: safety-critical fault (throttle-by-wire, ECM integrity or oil pressure). Hiding its lamp means you will not be told when the ECU has gone into a throttle or engine fail-safe. Not recommended.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1B9698" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x01</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA003" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P2120 - APS sensor 1 circuit - MIL enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the MIL when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 2, lamp byte @0x1B96AC (mask 0x01). CAUTION: safety-critical fault (throttle-by-wire, ECM integrity or oil pressure). Hiding its lamp means you will not be told when the ECU has gone into a throttle or engine fail-safe. Not recommended.

