n B2 [emissions - label only]</title><description>Emissions-related DTC, DTC index 116. Shown for reference only: this constant displays the DTC number stored in the record (hex, no P prefix), not the lamp byte. Stock lamp group: MIL. Record @0x1B9F88. No lamp toggle is provided for emissions monitors.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="50" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1B9F89" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>DTC (hex)</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xA076" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P0175 #2 - Fuel system too rich B2 [emissions - label only]</title><description>Emissions-related DTC, DTC index 117. Shown for reference only: this constant displays the DTC number stored in the record (hex, no P prefix), not the lamp byte. Stock lamp group: MIL. Record @0x1B9F9C. No lamp toggle is provided for emissions monitors.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="50" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1B9F9D" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>DTC (hex)</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xA077" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P050B - Cold-start ignition timing performance [emissions - label only]</title><description>Emissions-related DTC, DTC index 118. Shown for reference only: this constant displays the DTC number stored in the record (hex, no P prefix), not the lamp byte. Stock lamp group: MIL. Record @0x1B9FB0. No lamp toggle is provided for emissions monitors.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="50" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1B9FB1" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>DTC (hex)</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA078" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P1650 - Suzuki P1650 (warning-lamp code) - Warning lamp enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the Warning lamp when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 119, lamp byte @0x1B9FD0 (mask 0x40).

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1B9FD0" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x40</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA079" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P0602 - ECM programming error - none (group 0x10) enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the MIL when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 120, lamp byte @0x1B9FE4 (mask 0x01). CAUTION: safety-critical fault (throttle-by-wire, ECM integrity or oil pressure). Hiding its lamp means you will not be told when the ECU has gone into a throttle or engine fail-safe. Not recommended. Stock lamp byte is 0x10, which already lights no lamp through these paths. Ticking this sets bit0, which turns the MIL on.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1B9FE4" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x01</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA07A" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P1622 - ECM EEPROM error - MIL enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the MIL when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 121, lamp byte @0x1B9FF8 (mask 0x01). CAUTION: safety-critical fault (throttle-by-wire, ECM integrity or oil pressure). Hiding its lamp means you will not be told when the ECU has gone into a throttle or engine fail-safe. Not recommended.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1B9FF8" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x01</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA07B" flags="0x0"><title>DTC U0073 - CAN bus off - Warning lamp enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the Warning lamp when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 122, lamp byte @0x1BA00C (mask 0x40). ABS-DELETE RELATED: this code sets when the ABS unit, IMU or wheel-speed signals are missing.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1BA00C" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x40</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA07C" flags="0x0"><title>DTC U0121 - Lost communication with ABS unit - Warning lamp enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the Warning lamp when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 123, lamp byte @0x1BA020 (mask 0x40). ABS-DELETE RELATED: this code sets when the ABS unit, IMU or wheel-speed signals are missing.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1BA020" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x40</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA07D" flags="0x0"><title>DTC U0123 - Lost communication with IMU - Warning lamp enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the Warning lamp when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 124, lamp byte @0x1BA034 (mask 0x40). ABS-DELETE RELATED: this code sets when the ABS unit, IMU or wheel-speed signals are missing.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1BA034" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x40</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA07E" flags="0x0"><title>DTC U0155 - Lost communication with instrument cluster - Warning lamp enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the Warning lamp when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 125, lamp byte @0x1BA048 (mask 0x40).

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1BA048" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x40</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA07F" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P2158 #4 - Vehicle speed sensor B (rear wheel speed from ABS unit) - MIL enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the MIL when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 126, lamp byte @0x1BA05C (mask 0x01). ABS-DELETE RELATED: this code sets when the ABS unit, IMU or wheel-speed signals are missing.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1BA05C" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x01</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xA080" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P0130 #2 - HO2 sensor B1S1 circuit [emissions - label only]</title><description>Emissions-related DTC, DTC index 127. Shown for reference only: this constant displays the DTC number stored in the record (hex, no P prefix), not the lamp byte. Stock lamp group: MIL. Record @0x1BA064. No lamp toggle is provided for emissions monitors.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="50" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1BA065" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>DTC (hex)</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xA081" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P0150 #2 - HO2 sensor B2S1 circuit [emissions - label only]</title><description>Emissions-related DTC, DTC index 128. Shown for reference only: this constant displays the DTC number stored in the record (hex, no P prefix), not the lamp byte. Stock lamp group: MIL. Record @0x1BA078. No lamp toggle is provided for emissions monitors.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="50" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1BA079" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>DTC (hex)</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA082" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P0520 - Engine oil pressure sensor/switch circuit (not in Gen3 manual) - MIL enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the MIL when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 129, lamp byte @0x1BA098 (mask 0x01). CAUTION: safety-critical fault (throttle-by-wire, ECM integrity or oil pressure). Hiding its lamp means you will not be told when the ECU has gone into a throttle or engine fail-safe. Not recommended.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1BA098" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x01</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xA083" flags="0x0"><title>DTC P0522 - Engine oil pressure sensor/switch low (not in Gen3 manual) - MIL enabled</title><description>Ticked = this DTC lights the MIL when it sets (stock). Unticked = the code still sets and is stored, but no lamp lights. DTC index 130, lamp byte @0x1BA0AC (mask 0x01). CAUTION: safety-critical fault (throttle-by-wire, ECM integrity or oil pressure). Hiding its lamp means you will not be told when the ECU has gone into a throttle or engine fail-safe. Not recommended.

HOW IT WORKS: each DTC has a 20-byte record in the diagnostic table at 0x1B9678 (131 records). Byte +0x0C of the record is the lamp group: 0x01 = MIL. FUN_938A8 moves the DTC into classes 6-8, which FUN_99E2A turns into the MIL request. 0x40 (or 0x80) = master warning lamp only (FUN_941AC). 0x00 = no lamp. Unticking the flag only stops the lamp. The DTC is still stored, still readable with a scan tool, and the ECU still runs its fail-safe for that fault (for example, P0500 still turns off traction control).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="49" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1BA0AC" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><mask>0x01</mask></XDFFLAG><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB001" flags="0x0"><title>MAP IAP - GAIN (slope)</title><description>IAP (manifold) sensor GAIN. FUN_742E2: counts = 7862 + (OFFSET-0x8000) + rawADC*GAIN*32/DIV, clamped 0..65535. DIV is a code immediate at 0x74302: stock 21850 (0x555A), SD-v3 10925 (0x2AAD) so a 3-bar sensor fits the stock internal scale (393.14 counts/kPa, 7862 = 0 kPa).
For a sensor kPa = a x rawADC + b:  GAIN = round(393.14 x a x DIV / 32),  OFFSET = round(32768 + 393.14 x b).
SD-v3 (a = 0.307429, b = -12.6): GAIN 41263 (0xA12F), OFFSET 27814 (0x6CA6). Internal IAP saturates at ~147 kPa - by design; SD fuel and boost spark read the raw ADC instead.
Keep 1023 x GAIN x 32 &lt; 2^31 (GAIN &lt; 65599).

STOCK: 0x81AA (33194). ADDRESS 0x18EF58, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="51" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18EF58" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB002" flags="0x0"><title>MAP IAP - OFFSET (zero)</title><description>IAP (manifold) sensor OFFSET - see IAP GAIN for the formula. SD-v3: 27814 (0x6CA6) for b = -12.6 kPa.

STOCK: 0x8000 (32768). ADDRESS 0x18EF5A, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="51" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18EF5A" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB003" flags="0x0"><title>MAP AP (baro) - GAIN (slope)</title><description>AP (baro) sensor GAIN. FUN_73FD2: counts = OFFSET + ((rawADC x GAIN)/50 &lt;&lt; 5)/437. Stock sensor is kept, so SD-v3 keeps STOCK (SD-v1/v2 had rescaled this, which broke every baro-indexed table).

STOCK: 0x81AA (33194). ADDRESS 0x18EF5E, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="51" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18EF5E" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB004" flags="0x0"><title>MAP AP (baro) - OFFSET (zero)</title><description>AP (baro) sensor OFFSET. SD-v3 = STOCK.

STOCK: 0x1EB7 (7863). ADDRESS 0x18EF60, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="51" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18EF60" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC001" flags="0x0"><title>Injector Global Size Scaler (K)</title><description>Global pulsewidth multiplier applied to every primary AND secondary pulse in FUN_4714C: time = deadtime + fuel_time x (K-400)/200. Displayed here as the factor. Stock K=600 = 1.00. FOR LARGER INJECTORS: factor = old_flow / new_flow (e.g. stock to 2x-flow injectors -&gt; 0.50 -&gt; K=500). Fit with matching deadtime tables. This is the cleanest single injector-size knob.

STOCK: 600 (0x258). ADDRESS 0x1824C8, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1824C8" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>factor</units><decimalpl>3</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="(X-400)/200"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC002" flags="0x0"><title>Injector Primary Flow Trim - Cyl 1</title><description>Per-cylinder primary-injector quantity-to-time scaler in FUN_460F6 (primary time = qty x split x this / 2^23). Stock 132. Proportional: lower = less fuel on cylinder 1. Use for per-cylinder balance or, alternatively to K, to rescale primaries only.

STOCK: 132 (0x84). ADDRESS 0x1826EF, 8-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1826EF" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC003" flags="0x0"><title>Injector Primary Flow Trim - Cyl 2</title><description>Per-cylinder primary-injector quantity-to-time scaler in FUN_460F6 (primary time = qty x split x this / 2^23). Stock 132. Proportional: lower = less fuel on cylinder 2. Use for per-cylinder balance or, alternatively to K, to rescale primaries only.

STOCK: 132 (0x84). ADDRESS 0x1826F0, 8-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1826F0" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC004" flags="0x0"><title>Injector Primary Flow Trim - Cyl 3</title><description>Per-cylinder primary-injector quantity-to-time scaler in FUN_460F6 (primary time = qty x split x this / 2^23). Stock 132. Proportional: lower = less fuel on cylinder 3. Use for per-cylinder balance or, alternatively to K, to rescale primaries only.

STOCK: 132 (0x84). ADDRESS 0x1826F1, 8-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1826F1" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC005" flags="0x0"><title>Injector Primary Flow Trim - Cyl 4</title><description>Per-cylinder primary-injector quantity-to-time scaler in FUN_460F6 (primary time = qty x split x this / 2^23). Stock 132. Proportional: lower = less fuel on cylinder 4. Use for per-cylinder balance or, alternatively to K, to rescale primaries only.

STOCK: 132 (0x84). ADDRESS 0x1826F2, 8-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1826F2" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC006" flags="0x0"><title>Injector Secondary Flow Scaler</title><description>Secondary (showerhead) injector quantity-to-time scaler in FUN_460F6 (secondary time = qty x split x this / 2^22). Stock 104. Rescale if you change the secondary injectors only.

STOCK: 104 (0x68). ADDRESS 0x1826F3, 8-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1826F3" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC007" flags="0x0"><title>Injector Pulsewidth Minimum</title><description>Lower clamp on computed injector time before deadtime (FUN_460F6), microseconds.

STOCK: 250 (0xFA). ADDRESS 0x1825FC, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1825FC" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>us</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC008" flags="0x0"><title>Injector Pulsewidth Maximum</title><description>Upper clamp on computed injector time before deadtime (FUN_460F6), microseconds (stock 25,000 = 25 ms). Check against your max-RPM injection window if you raise fueling a lot.

STOCK: 25000 (0x61A8). ADDRESS 0x1825FE, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1825FE" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>us</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC009" flags="0x0"><title>Fuel Blend - WOT Throttle-Path Gate</title><description>Above this throttle angle (fef02604) the ECU forces 100% throttle-path (alpha-N) fueling (FUN_4916E/FUN_491BC). Stock 91.4 deg. SD-v2 sets 0xFFFF (disabled) so speed density holds at WOT/boost.

STOCK: 33282 (0x8202). ADDRESS 0x1824C6, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="53" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1824C6" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>deg</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/364.08"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC00A" flags="0x0"><title>Neutral/Clutch Fuel-Map Gate</title><description>Pressure gate used by FUN_4543E (neutral/clutch fuel map allowed only if input &gt;= gate) and FUN_455E6 (neutral dwell counter, input = vacuum fef02628). SD-v3: FUN_4543E input is the raw IAP ADC (0-1023), so this must stay 0 or the neutral map is never used. Side effect vs stock: the neutral/clutch-in map also stays active under boost (stock dropped it at IAP &gt;= baro); those maps are boost-capable.

STOCK: 7863 (0x1EB7). ADDRESS 0x182626, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="53" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x182626" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC00C" flags="0x0"><title>IAP Sensor Circuit-Low Threshold (raw ADC)</title><description>Raw IAP ADC below which the circuit-low DTC starts debouncing (FUN_39076). Unchanged.

STOCK: 20. ADDRESS 0x1547E0, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="53" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1547E0" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC00B" flags="0x0"><title>IAP Sensor Circuit-High Threshold (raw ADC)</title><description>Raw IAP ADC (fef02574) above which the circuit-high DTC starts debouncing (FUN_390F8/FUN_3917A, debounce 0x1547E6 = 750). Stock 983 (~4.8 V) = ~290 kPa on the 3-bar sensor, which would fault under high boost. SD-v3: 1022 (only a shorted/saturated sensor trips).

STOCK: 983. ADDRESS 0x1547E2, 16-bit.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="53" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1547E2" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD001" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Enable</title><description>128 (0x80) = rolling anti-lag enabled; anything else = disabled (START button behaves stock: launch control long-press works again). Default 128.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF000" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD002" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Min Coolant Temp</title><description>ALS will not arm below this coolant temperature (RAM 0xFEF026BD). Default 60 C.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF001" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>deg C</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X*0.9375-30"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD003" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Min Rolling Speed</title><description>ALS arms only while the FRONT wheel speed (RAM 0xFEF0263A) is at or above this. Below it, holding START keeps its stock launch-control function. Default 20 km/h.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF002" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>km/h</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/128"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD004" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Capture Grip Angle (WOT)</title><description>With START held and rolling, the moment grip angle (RAM 0xFEF025EC, abs. accel angle; ~107 deg = full) reaches this, the current RPM is captured and held. Default 90 deg.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF004" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>deg grip</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/364.08"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD005" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Release Grip Angle</title><description>If the grip drops below this while active, ALS releases (re-opening past the capture angle re-captures). Default 60 deg. Keep below the capture angle.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF006" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>deg grip</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/364.08"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD006" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Min Capture RPM</title><description>ALS will not engage if RPM at capture is below this (avoids bogging at low RPM). Default 3000. Must be greater than the hysteresis.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF008" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD007" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Max Capture RPM</title><description>Captured RPM is clamped to this. Keep below the in-gear fuel-cut limiter (11,200 stock) and the ignition-cut limiter (12,000). Default 10500.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF00A" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD008" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Hold Hysteresis</title><description>Spark returns when RPM falls this far below the captured RPM (cut is ON at &gt;= captured RPM). Smaller = tighter hold, harsher cut. Default 150 rpm.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF00C" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT><XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD009" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Max Active Time</title><description>Safety timer: after this long continuously active, ALS drops out and stays off until START is released. Counted in the ~5 ms task (period inferred, verify on the bench). Default 2000 counts = 10 s.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF00E" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>s</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X*0.005"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT></XDFFORMAT>